WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.934
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:04.868
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:09.300
♪♪

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.400
Let's get to some news,
you guys.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.901
Last night, President Biden

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.834
did a rare sit-down interview
on "60 Minutes."

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:15.000
I don't know if you saw this.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.234
And he made a pretty big
announcement.

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:17.767
In case you missed it,
here it is.

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:19.834
-Is the pandemic over?

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:21.968
-The pandemic is over.

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:23.834
We still have a problem
with COVID.

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:26.400
We're still doing
a lot of work on it.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.567
It's --
But the pandemic is over.

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:31.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:36.033
-It's kind of huge news to
mention so casually, you know?

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:38.601
I wasn't expecting the end of a
two-and-a-half-year nightmare

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:41.567
to be announced on the floor
of the Detroit Auto Show.

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:44.400
It's like hearing,
"I had a good day.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.367
Went for a run, ate breakfast,
the baby was born, you know."

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:54.267
Apparently Biden's comment was
not part of his planned remarks

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:57.567
and caught several of his own
health officials by surprise.

00:00:57.567 --> 00:00:59.067
Dr. Fauci was like, "Oh, God.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:01.200
it's 2020 all over again.
Oh, my God."

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.767
For the rest of the interview,

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:04.267
whenever Biden
answered a question,

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:05.901
a staffer quickly revved
a car engine.

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:08.367
He's like, "That's right. We're
going to go to war with Ch--"

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:10.400
[ Engine revs, tires screech ]

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:11.667
"We're gonna support Tai--"

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.701
[ Engine revs, tires screech ]

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:16.434
Later in the interview, Biden,
though, was asked about his age.

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:17.801
Watch this.

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:21.934
-Mr. President, you are
the oldest president ever.

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:23.567
-Pretty good shape, huh?

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:25.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.634
[ Applause ]

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:30.501
-He handled it pretty well,
yeah.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:32.567
Although, I will say it got
a little dicey after that.

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:33.834
Take a look at this.

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:36.667
-How would you say
your mental focus is?

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:39.467
-Oh, it's focused.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:41.701
I say -- I think it's --
I -- I haven't -- Look.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.734
You think I would tell you
if I knew exactly?

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:45.400
Of course
I'm not going to tell you.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:48.601
So I -- Look.
This is a process.

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:49.934
This is a process.

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:51.634
And the proof of the pudding's
in the eating.

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:56.901
I mean, don't -- don't -- don't.

00:01:56.901 --> 00:02:00.968
My point is, it takes time.
How's an old guy do that?

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:03.634
I no more think of myself
as being as old as I am

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:05.334
than a fly.

00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:06.467
-What do you mean?

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:08.033
-No.

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:10.167
-No, man. Yo, yo, yo. Yo!

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:11.734
-That's edited, right?

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:14.634
-No.
-Alright. Thank you.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.234
-That's a joke.
-No, that's not real.

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:18.367
-Oh God.

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:20.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.834
-Props to our editors there.

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:24.367
Well, I saw that this weekend

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:27.267
former president Trump
spoke at a rally in Ohio,

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:28.634
and at one point
during his speech,

00:02:28.634 --> 00:02:30.167
music started playing,

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:31.868
and his supporters reacted
in a pretty strange way.

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.267
Check this out.

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:35.934
-And a Department of Justice
that refuses to investigate

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:38.300
egregious acts...
[ Grand, sweeping music plays ]

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.267
...of voting irregularities
and fraud.

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:45.300
And we have a president
who is cognitively impaired

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:48.868
and in no condition
to lead our country.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.133
-Not creepy at all.

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:53.167
Then Trump was like,

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:55.667
"And now to sacrifice
the first-born sons.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.968
Come up here, Don Jr."

00:02:57.968 --> 00:03:00.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:02.067
What was going on?

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:04.200
Meanwhile, Trump just returned
to Mar-a-lago

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.467
for the first time
since the FBI search,

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:09.000
and he's complaining
that FBI agents

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.868
didn't even take off their shoes
before going into his bedroom.

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:14.834
Yeah, for some reason,

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:16.968
the agents weren't like,
"FBI! This is a raid!"

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:20.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:22.968
"Should have wore Velcro."

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:24.501
Of course, everyone is talking
about this today --

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:26.067
leaders, dignitaries,
and politicians

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:28.100
from around the world
gathered in London

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.767
for the funeral
of Queen Elizabeth.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:31.734
Meanwhile, Trump showed up
at a Burger King

00:03:31.734 --> 00:03:33.567
and said,
"Sorry for your loss."

00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:36.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:40.767
"Two whoppers.
French fries. Diet Coke."

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:43.534
[ Applause ]

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:45.601
In observance for the funeral,

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:48.067
flights in and out of
London's Heathrow Airport

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:50.300
were canceled or delayed.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.868
LaGuardia heard that
and was like,

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:54.901
"Uh, that's also why our
flights are, uh..."

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:57.734
[ Clears throat ]
"Out of respect, of course.

00:03:57.734 --> 00:03:59.367
We're gonna be respecting
till, like,

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:01.400
around New Year's, probably.
That's what was...

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.667
We'll continue our respect.
Yeah."

00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:06.000
Some entertainment news --
we're just one month away

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.701
from the release
of Taylor Swift's

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:09.400
10th studio album, "Midnights."

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:15.901
And fans are already finding
all kinds of secret messages

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.934
about the album
in her social-media posts.

00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:20.834
-Oh, man, all that stuff is just
conspiracy theories, though.

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.334
-Uh, I don't know, Tariq.
The clues are --

00:04:22.334 --> 00:04:25.601
The clues are everywhere.
-What clues?

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:27.467
-Okay, so, Taylor made
a surprise announcement

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.400
at this year's VMAs
that her 10th studio album

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.701
was gonna be called "Midnights"

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:33.234
and it would come out
at midnight on October 21st.

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:34.934
You follow?
-Uh...

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:37.067
-So, 13 is Taylor's
favorite number,

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:39.000
and "Midnights" is gonna have
13 tracks on it,

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.968
but nobody knows
what the songs are called yet.

00:04:40.968 --> 00:04:42.701
On all the album art
she's shared so far,

00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:44.200
all the songs have fake titles

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.334
like "Track One," "Track Two,"
that kind of thing.

00:04:46.334 --> 00:04:49.000
-And that means...?
-But when she posted a video

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.267
announcing all of
the limited-edition vinyls,

00:04:51.267 --> 00:04:53.467
the names of the songs were
all blurred out on the covers,

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:54.934
so you can tell the songs
won't actually be called

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:57.000
"Track One," "Track Two."
And that was on September 1st.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.467
Then on September 16th,

00:04:58.467 --> 00:04:59.901
she posted another video
revealing

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:03.133
that if you line up the backs of
all the special-edition vinyls

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:05.801
with the regular-edition one,
it makes a clock.

00:05:05.801 --> 00:05:07.834
Midnight is a time on a clock.

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:11.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:13.567
-Okay. Okay, well, I guess --
-Yeah, but here --

00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:15.167
here's where
it gets interesting.

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:17.434
In Taylor's entire discography,

00:05:17.434 --> 00:05:19.868
she's only sung the word
"midnight" in six songs.

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.901
She sings it in "Style"
off of "1989,"

00:05:21.901 --> 00:05:23.300
"You Are in Love" off of "1989,"

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.734
"New Year's Day"
off of "Reputation,"

00:05:24.734 --> 00:05:26.400
"The Last Great American
Dynasty" off "Folklore,"

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:27.734
"Happiness" off of "Evermore,"

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:29.334
and, of course,
in "22 (Taylor's Version)"

00:05:29.334 --> 00:05:30.601
off "Red (Taylor's Version)."

00:05:30.601 --> 00:05:31.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:33.634
And that's not even
the crazy part.

00:05:33.634 --> 00:05:36.334
'Cause it also turns out
she's sung the phrase
"middle of the night"

00:05:36.334 --> 00:05:38.167
in seven songs
throughout her discography.

00:05:38.167 --> 00:05:40.267
She sings it in "...Ready
For It?" off "Reputation,"

00:05:40.267 --> 00:05:41.501
"Daylight" off of "Lover,"

00:05:41.501 --> 00:05:42.834
"You Belong with Me
(Taylor's Version)"

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:44.267
off of
"Fearless (Taylor's Version),"

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:45.400
"Untouchable
(Taylor's Version),"

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.701
off of "Fearless
(Taylor's Version),"

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:48.501
"All Too Well (10 Minute
Version) (Taylor's Version)"

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:50.033
off of "Red (Taylor's Version),"

00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:51.234
"Better Man
(Taylor's Version)"

00:05:51.234 --> 00:05:52.767
off of "Red (Taylor's Version),"

00:05:52.767 --> 00:05:55.000
and "Nothing New
(feat. Phoebe Bridgers)
(Taylor's version)"

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.667
off of "Red (Taylor's Version)."

00:05:56.667 --> 00:06:00.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:01.868
-What are you even saying?!

00:06:01.868 --> 00:06:04.968
-Six "midnights" plus seven
"middle of the nights"

00:06:04.968 --> 00:06:07.300
equal...13.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.200
13 is Taylor's favorite number.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:11.167
That's how many songs
are on "Midnights."

00:06:11.167 --> 00:06:12.701
Taylor's a genius!

00:06:12.701 --> 00:06:15.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:15.167 --> 00:06:16.968
That's what.

00:06:16.968 --> 00:06:19.100
You get it now?
-Yeah, I get it.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:21.801
Happy birthday.
-Thank you. I appreciate it.

00:06:21.801 --> 00:06:23.334
Well, this is going viral.

00:06:23.334 --> 00:06:26.634
Guys, an 80-year-old
state Senate candidate in Utah

00:06:26.634 --> 00:06:28.501
named Linda Paulson
is going viral

00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:31.067
because of a new campaign video
that she just released.

00:06:31.067 --> 00:06:32.434
Can we see this, please?

00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:35.968
♪♪

00:06:35.968 --> 00:06:37.901
-Oh, no.

00:06:37.901 --> 00:06:40.834
-♪ Hey, Utah District 12,
listen up right here ♪

00:06:40.834 --> 00:06:42.300
♪ There's a new name
on the ballot ♪

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.000
♪ For the Senate this year ♪

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.067
♪ My name is Linda Paulson,
Republican and awesome ♪

00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:49.734
-Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:49.734 --> 00:06:52.467
-At that point, the Tupac
hologram unplugged itself.

00:06:52.467 --> 00:06:54.701
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.701 --> 00:06:57.133
It's like if "Hamilton"
was written by Mike Pence.

00:06:57.133 --> 00:06:58.501
Doesn't it kind of...?

00:06:58.501 --> 00:07:01.400
And finally, guys, do you
ever see a photo in the news

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:02.901
and think that headline
should be different?

00:07:02.901 --> 00:07:04.267
Well, we'll take care
of that right now.

00:07:04.267 --> 00:07:07.067
It's time for "News and
Improved." Here we go.

00:07:07.067 --> 00:07:12.367
-♪ News and Improved ♪

00:07:12.367 --> 00:07:15.400
-For example, check out --
check out this first photo here.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.267
The original headline was...

00:07:21.901 --> 00:07:24.167
Headline could have been...

00:07:27.801 --> 00:07:32.334
[ Applause ]

00:07:32.334 --> 00:07:34.133
The next headline was...

00:07:36.801 --> 00:07:38.534
Headline could have been...

00:07:43.501 --> 00:07:47.467
"No one's getting fired."

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:49.167
This next headline was...

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.968
Headline could have been...

00:07:56.167 --> 00:07:57.467
[ Applause ]

00:07:57.467 --> 00:08:01.267
[ Laughs ]
"Oh, yeah. This was back..."

00:08:01.267 --> 00:08:03.968
-"I coulda.
I didn't. But I coulda."

00:08:03.968 --> 00:08:05.167
-"I didn't, but I coulda."

00:08:05.167 --> 00:08:07.334
"Are you sure?"

00:08:07.334 --> 00:08:10.968
Next headline was...

00:08:10.968 --> 00:08:13.000
Headline could have been...

00:08:15.567 --> 00:08:17.467
[ Laughter ]

00:08:17.467 --> 00:08:20.567
[ Applause ]

00:08:20.567 --> 00:08:22.767
-Wow!

00:08:22.767 --> 00:08:24.667
That's a headline.

00:08:24.667 --> 00:08:28.868
-Next headline was...

00:08:28.868 --> 00:08:30.801
Headline could have been...

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:37.234
[ Applause ]

00:08:37.234 --> 00:08:41.434
Next headline was...

00:08:41.434 --> 00:08:43.734
Headline could have been...

00:08:47.467 --> 00:08:49.234
[ Applause ]

00:08:52.501 --> 00:08:56.133
Next headline was...

00:08:56.133 --> 00:08:58.000
Headline could have been...

00:09:00.934 --> 00:09:02.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:02.467 --> 00:09:04.467
-Wow!

00:09:04.467 --> 00:09:06.667
[ Applause ]

00:09:06.667 --> 00:09:11.934
-And finally,
this headline was...

00:09:11.934 --> 00:09:15.334
Headline could have been...

00:09:17.701 --> 00:09:20.067
It's a busy time
in New York City because leaders

00:09:20.067 --> 00:09:21.934
from all around the world
are in town

00:09:21.934 --> 00:09:24.734
for the U.N. General Assembly.
Yeah.

00:09:24.734 --> 00:09:27.400
And I just want to say
on behalf of all New Yorkers,

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.701
this could have been a Zoom.

00:09:28.701 --> 00:09:30.868
[ Laughter ]

00:09:30.868 --> 00:09:32.400
Have we learned nothing?

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.033
[ Applause ]

00:09:34.033 --> 00:09:36.200
Two and a half hours
to go three blocks?

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.567
What are we doing, people?

00:09:38.567 --> 00:09:40.934
Yeah, this is the first
in-person General Assembly

00:09:40.934 --> 00:09:43.100
since the pandemic.
That's right.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.067
For the last three years,
the U.N. has been home

00:09:45.067 --> 00:09:47.334
to the world's largest
Spirit Halloween.

00:09:47.334 --> 00:09:48.667
[ Laughter ]

00:09:48.667 --> 00:09:51.100
Fun fact. Fun fact. Fun fact.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:53.033
[ Applause ]

00:09:53.033 --> 00:09:55.667
That's right.
Today leaders from 193 nations

00:09:55.667 --> 00:09:57.934
flew into New York
on private jets

00:09:57.934 --> 00:10:00.200
and drove into the U.N.
in huge motorcades

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:03.000
all with one shared goal --
to fight climate change.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.133
[ Laughter ]

00:10:08.367 --> 00:10:11.033
Honestly, I love when the U.N.
General Assembly is in session.

00:10:11.033 --> 00:10:13.434
There's no greater joy than
watching the king of Norway

00:10:13.434 --> 00:10:15.267
getting into a fight
with his Uber driver.

00:10:15.267 --> 00:10:16.767
You know? It's just magic.

00:10:16.767 --> 00:10:19.467
There's a magic spirit
in the air.

00:10:19.467 --> 00:10:22.000
For several days,
there will be dozens of speeches

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:24.534
at the U.N.,
and the after-party --

00:10:24.534 --> 00:10:26.801
Ron DeSantis is transporting
all the foreign leaders

00:10:26.801 --> 00:10:28.334
to Martha's Vineyard.

00:10:28.334 --> 00:10:29.734
-Aww.
-Isn't that nice?

00:10:29.734 --> 00:10:32.767
That's nice. Very thoughtful.

00:10:32.767 --> 00:10:35.634
[ Applause ]

00:10:35.634 --> 00:10:39.000
Actually, tomorrow President
Biden will speak at the U.N.

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:41.601
He's part of the long lineup
of leaders from across the world

00:10:41.601 --> 00:10:43.200
who will be making remarks.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.100
Let's take a look at what
their speeches are about.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:47.767
For instance, here's
the president of Portugal.

00:10:47.767 --> 00:10:51.033
Yep, he's speaking about how
every dinner party he attends

00:10:51.033 --> 00:10:53.200
turns into a murder mystery.

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:55.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:55.267 --> 00:10:58.534
-What?
-"I wouldn't know!"

00:10:58.534 --> 00:11:00.601
Next up, here's the
president of South Korea.

00:11:00.601 --> 00:11:02.400
He's speaking about
all the hot goss

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:04.434
from the "Don't Worry Darling"
press tour.

00:11:04.434 --> 00:11:06.634
[ Laughter ]

00:11:06.634 --> 00:11:08.968
[ Applause ]

00:11:08.968 --> 00:11:11.300
Next up,
here's the leader of Finland.

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:12.801
Yeah, he's speaking about

00:11:12.801 --> 00:11:16.000
reacting to good news
by saying, "MmmmmMMMYESSS."

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.501
[ Laughter ]

00:11:17.501 --> 00:11:20.667
[ Applause ]

00:11:20.667 --> 00:11:23.367
Next up,
here's the president of Brazil.

00:11:23.367 --> 00:11:25.100
He's speaking about
how easy it is

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:26.934
to steel sashes
from Girl Scouts.

00:11:26.934 --> 00:11:29.133
You go, "Well, that's --
It shouldn't be that easy."

00:11:29.133 --> 00:11:31.067
It shouldn't be that easy.

00:11:31.067 --> 00:11:33.234
Next up,
here's the leader of Germany.

00:11:33.234 --> 00:11:35.033
He's speaking
about that time he spent

00:11:35.033 --> 00:11:37.467
playing the dad
on "That '70s Show."

00:11:37.467 --> 00:11:39.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:39.734 --> 00:11:41.901
Lots of speeches.

00:11:41.901 --> 00:11:43.567
Here's the president of Latvia.

00:11:43.567 --> 00:11:45.567
He's speaking about mustaches

00:11:45.567 --> 00:11:47.501
that age slower
than the rest of your head.

00:11:47.501 --> 00:11:49.167
-Oh.

00:11:49.167 --> 00:11:51.167
[ Applause ]

00:11:51.167 --> 00:11:53.434
-Next up,
here's the president of Chile.

00:11:53.434 --> 00:11:55.334
He's speaking about
looking more like

00:11:55.334 --> 00:11:57.334
the president of
Royal Caribbean Cruise Lines.

00:11:57.334 --> 00:11:59.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:02.467 --> 00:12:04.701
And, finally, here's Joe Biden.

00:12:04.701 --> 00:12:06.801
He's speaking about
the Showcase Showdown

00:12:06.801 --> 00:12:08.868
and getting your pet
spayed or neutered.

00:12:08.868 --> 00:12:11.601
[ "Price is Right" theme plays ]

00:12:11.601 --> 00:12:13.534
-Come on down!

00:12:13.534 --> 00:12:18.667
♪♪

00:12:18.667 --> 00:12:20.601
-Uh, did you guys
see this yesterday

00:12:20.601 --> 00:12:22.000
at the Queen's funeral?

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:25.200
President Biden was there.
He was seated in the 14th row.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:28.067
Well, former president Trump
noticed, and he said...

00:12:31.133 --> 00:12:33.400
[ Laughter ]

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:34.834
Yeah.

00:12:34.834 --> 00:12:36.467
Yeah, at funerals, Trump demands

00:12:36.467 --> 00:12:39.033
to be seated directly on top of
the coffin or he won't --

00:12:39.033 --> 00:12:41.267
he won't show up.

00:12:41.267 --> 00:12:44.467
[as Trump]
"I gotta be right there.

00:12:44.467 --> 00:12:46.534
I don't care
if it's open or closed."

00:12:46.534 --> 00:12:48.834
[ Laughter ]

00:12:48.834 --> 00:12:50.133
-"Me!"

00:12:50.133 --> 00:12:52.334
-Yeah, Biden was
in the 14th row.

00:12:52.334 --> 00:12:53.767
Even worse, he got stuck behind

00:12:53.767 --> 00:12:55.601
one of those royal guards
with the giant fuzzy hats.

00:12:55.601 --> 00:12:58.734
He's like, "Alright.
Why even invite me? Come on."

00:12:58.734 --> 00:13:00.367
But that wasn't all that Trump

00:13:00.367 --> 00:13:02.133
had to say about
where Biden was seated.

00:13:02.133 --> 00:13:03.734
He also said...

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:09.734
Biden was like, "He's right.

00:13:09.734 --> 00:13:12.033
Whether it's funerals
or classified documents,

00:13:12.033 --> 00:13:15.467
location is everything."

00:13:15.467 --> 00:13:16.968
[ Laughter ]

00:13:16.968 --> 00:13:18.634
♪♪

00:13:18.634 --> 00:13:22.300
"You're correct.
It is everything."

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:24.000
Well, people are
talking about this.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:26.300
The chief operating officer
of Beyond Meat --

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:28.534
this is a real story --

00:13:28.534 --> 00:13:30.968
was just arrested
for a really strange reason.

00:13:30.968 --> 00:13:32.133
Check this out.

00:13:32.133 --> 00:13:34.868
-The COO of Beyond Meat
is facing charges

00:13:34.868 --> 00:13:38.801
for biting a man's nose after
a football game in Arkansas.

00:13:38.801 --> 00:13:41.534
[ Laughter ]

00:13:41.534 --> 00:13:44.067
-Yes!
-And in a blind taste test,

00:13:44.067 --> 00:13:46.467
he said he couldn't tell
the difference between a nose

00:13:46.467 --> 00:13:48.434
and a Beyond Meat nose.

00:13:48.434 --> 00:13:50.701
-Wow.
-Can't even tell the difference.

00:13:50.701 --> 00:13:52.834
Well, switching gears,
I heard that the latest

00:13:52.834 --> 00:13:57.033
Gen Z fashion trend is wearing
jeans with the button undone.

00:13:57.033 --> 00:13:59.033
-Ooh.
-Yeah, which means after

00:13:59.033 --> 00:14:00.901
Thanksgiving dinner, every uncle
Is going to be like,

00:14:00.901 --> 00:14:04.567
"Ohh. I look like
Gigi freaking Hadid over here!

00:14:04.567 --> 00:14:08.701
What am I -- What am I doin'?!
Hey!"

00:14:08.701 --> 00:14:10.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:14:10.367 --> 00:14:12.834
Let's get to some news.
Well, guys, today New York

00:14:12.834 --> 00:14:16.234
Attorney General Letitia James
announced a lawsuit against

00:14:16.234 --> 00:14:18.901
former president Trump
and his three adult children

00:14:18.901 --> 00:14:22.000
for allegedly committing
widespread business fraud.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.968
[ Audience oohs ]

00:14:23.968 --> 00:14:25.934
You can tell Trump's worried
because he just asked

00:14:25.934 --> 00:14:27.734
Ron DeSantis to fly him
somewhere random

00:14:27.734 --> 00:14:28.767
in the middle of the night.

00:14:28.767 --> 00:14:30.667
[ Laughter ]

00:14:30.667 --> 00:14:32.801
Trump is being accused
of exaggerating

00:14:32.801 --> 00:14:34.400
the value of his properties.

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:36.367
The attorney general
cited a few examples.

00:14:36.367 --> 00:14:38.734
One of them being that Trump
said Mar-a-Lago is worth

00:14:38.734 --> 00:14:43.501
$739 million, but it was only
appraised at $75 million.

00:14:43.501 --> 00:14:45.267
[ Laughter ]

00:14:45.267 --> 00:14:46.834
Trump was like,
"Technically, with all

00:14:46.834 --> 00:14:49.100
the classified documents,
it is worth $739 million."

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:55.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:14:55.467 --> 00:14:57.734
You took it out.

00:14:57.734 --> 00:15:01.801
Yep, $739 million, almost
10 times the actual value.

00:15:01.801 --> 00:15:04.067
Trump was going to put down
$740 million,

00:15:04.067 --> 00:15:05.667
but he didn't want to
arouse suspicion.

00:15:05.667 --> 00:15:07.501
[ Laughter ]

00:15:07.501 --> 00:15:09.834
In response to the alleged
fraud, the State of New York

00:15:09.834 --> 00:15:14.133
is now suing Trump
for $250 million.

00:15:14.133 --> 00:15:15.667
Trump was like, "$250 million?

00:15:15.667 --> 00:15:17.567
That's how much my fish tank
is appraised for."

00:15:17.567 --> 00:15:20.801
[ Laughter ]
"Alright. Just take the tank."

00:15:20.801 --> 00:15:23.400
Yes, Trump exaggerated the size
of his wealth,

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:24.868
his apartment,
and his properties.

00:15:24.868 --> 00:15:27.801
It's the first time he's ever
lied about how big something is.

00:15:27.801 --> 00:15:31.501
[ Laughter ]

00:15:31.501 --> 00:15:34.434
Other than his inauguration
crowd,

00:15:34.434 --> 00:15:35.868
his vote total,

00:15:35.868 --> 00:15:37.701
and his night with
Stormy Daniels.

00:15:37.701 --> 00:15:40.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:15:40.968 --> 00:15:43.300
"Take the fish tank.
Take the tank.

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:45.601
I hate to see it go."

00:15:45.601 --> 00:15:47.934
Yep, the attorney general laid
out all the details of

00:15:47.934 --> 00:15:50.534
Trump's alleged fraud, and then
she ended her press conference

00:15:50.534 --> 00:15:51.667
by saying this.

00:15:51.667 --> 00:15:55.367
-Claiming you have money
that you do not have

00:15:55.367 --> 00:15:59.367
does not amount to
"The Art of the Deal."

00:15:59.367 --> 00:16:01.334
It's the art of the steal.

00:16:01.334 --> 00:16:03.300
-Ooh.
[ Audience oohs ]

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:05.367
[ Rimshot ]

00:16:05.367 --> 00:16:07.434
That's a burn.
-Ooh.

00:16:07.434 --> 00:16:10.501
-That's an accidentally locking
yourself in a tanning bed burn.

00:16:10.501 --> 00:16:14.701
[ Laughter ]
"Help, help."

00:16:14.701 --> 00:16:17.400
Some more big news from here
in New York.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:18.834
This morning President Biden
addressed

00:16:18.834 --> 00:16:20.701
the U.N. General assembly.

00:16:20.701 --> 00:16:22.901
In his 30-minute speech,
Biden said we need peace

00:16:22.901 --> 00:16:25.100
between Russia and Ukraine
in Europe

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:27.367
and also Rachel and Tino
on "The Bachelorette."

00:16:27.367 --> 00:16:29.534
We need peace.
[ Laughter ]

00:16:29.534 --> 00:16:31.934
Yeah, Biden spent a good portion
of his speech on Russia.

00:16:31.934 --> 00:16:33.734
You can tell he was serious
because he was doing

00:16:33.734 --> 00:16:35.167
that weird whisper thing.

00:16:35.167 --> 00:16:38.167
[ Whispering ]
"That's why we do everything

00:16:38.167 --> 00:16:41.434
[Normal voice]
to defeat Russia!"

00:16:41.434 --> 00:16:43.534
I like that whisper thing
he does.

00:16:43.534 --> 00:16:45.300
[ Whispering ] "We've been
trying to raise money

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:47.100
the whole time.

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:48.767
[ Normal voice ]
Building more bridges!"

00:16:48.767 --> 00:16:50.601
[ Laughter ]

00:16:50.601 --> 00:16:54.100
Speaking of Russia, today
Vladimir Putin asked for 300,000

00:16:54.100 --> 00:16:55.501
more troops in Ukraine,

00:16:55.501 --> 00:16:58.501
and hinted that he hasn't ruled
out a nuclear response.

00:16:58.501 --> 00:17:00.400
The only thing missing
from Putin's speech was

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:02.133
a cat for him
to pet the whole time.

00:17:02.133 --> 00:17:04.100
[ Laughter ]

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.801
Even Kim Jong-un called.
He was like,

00:17:05.801 --> 00:17:07.133
"Dude, you're scaring me.
What's up?"

00:17:07.133 --> 00:17:09.167
[ Laughter ]
Let's switch gears.

00:17:09.167 --> 00:17:12.067
Guys, I heard that YouTube's
"dislike" and "not interested"

00:17:12.067 --> 00:17:14.467
buttons don't actually stop
the platform

00:17:14.467 --> 00:17:16.400
from showing you
similar content.

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:18.033
[ Laughter ]

00:17:18.033 --> 00:17:20.067
Yeah, they're basically
the elevator door-close

00:17:20.067 --> 00:17:21.100
buttons of the Internet.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:24.400
[ Laughter ]

00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:27.200
-He's coming, he's coming.
-Sorry.

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:30.467
I wish I could -- Ah!
Hi, how was your weekend?

00:17:30.467 --> 00:17:32.100
[ Laughter ]

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:34.467
Some entertainment news.
Apparently "House of the Dragon"

00:17:34.467 --> 00:17:37.567
is averaging 29 million viewers
per episode.

00:17:37.567 --> 00:17:38.901
-Ooh!

00:17:38.901 --> 00:17:40.334
-But now I think
all the networks are trying

00:17:40.334 --> 00:17:41.567
to get in on the action.

00:17:41.567 --> 00:17:43.000
I watched CNN this morning.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.200
Wolf Blitzer looks
a little different.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:45.834
Take a look.
Do you see what I'm saying?

00:17:45.834 --> 00:17:47.701
[ Laughter ]
They're all trying to do it.

00:17:47.701 --> 00:17:49.701
-It's crazy.
-Yeah.

00:17:49.701 --> 00:17:52.701
Hey, guys, I read that American
Airlines just announced hackers

00:17:52.701 --> 00:17:54.400
accessed
the personal information

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:56.400
of some of their customers.

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:57.734
But you can look at it this way.

00:17:57.734 --> 00:17:59.834
When they use your credit card,
you still get miles.

00:17:59.834 --> 00:18:02.234
[ Laughter ]
-Oh!

00:18:02.234 --> 00:18:04.868
-And finally, speaking of
airlines, I saw that Southwest

00:18:04.868 --> 00:18:08.033
surprised a full flight with
ukulele lessons

00:18:08.033 --> 00:18:10.167
on a trip
from California to Hawaii.

00:18:10.167 --> 00:18:11.734
Take a look at this.

00:18:11.734 --> 00:18:14.367
[ Laughter ]

00:18:14.367 --> 00:18:16.667
The person in front of
the emergency exit was like,

00:18:16.667 --> 00:18:17.801
"This counts, right?"

00:18:17.801 --> 00:18:19.033
[ Laughter ]

00:18:19.033 --> 00:18:20.868
They didn't just clap
when that plane landed.

00:18:20.868 --> 00:18:22.234
They gave him
a standing ovation.

00:18:22.234 --> 00:18:24.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:18:24.667 --> 00:18:26.133
Everyone is talking about this.

00:18:26.133 --> 00:18:27.501
Last night,
former president Trump

00:18:27.501 --> 00:18:29.868
was interviewed by Sean Hannity
on Fox News.

00:18:29.868 --> 00:18:31.400
And when Hannity
brought up Trump's claim

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:34.434
that he declassified the
documents found at Mar-a-Lago,

00:18:34.434 --> 00:18:36.501
Trump gave a very
interesting explanation.

00:18:36.501 --> 00:18:37.567
Take a look at this.

00:18:37.567 --> 00:18:38.767
-Is there a process?

00:18:38.767 --> 00:18:40.133
What was your process
to declassify?

00:18:40.133 --> 00:18:42.968
-There doesn't have to be
a process, as I understand it.

00:18:42.968 --> 00:18:44.801
You know, there's different --
People say different things.

00:18:44.801 --> 00:18:46.467
But, as I understand,
there doesn't have to be --

00:18:46.467 --> 00:18:48.167
If you're the
President of the United States,

00:18:48.167 --> 00:18:51.234
you can declassify just by
saying, "It's declassified,"

00:18:51.234 --> 00:18:52.567
even by thinking about it.

00:19:00.868 --> 00:19:02.367
-Hannity was like,
"Oh, I get it.

00:19:02.367 --> 00:19:03.567
You're going to plead insanity.

00:19:03.567 --> 00:19:06.501
Okay, now it's making sense."

00:19:06.501 --> 00:19:08.701
Meanwhile, Ron DeSantis
was watching at home going,

00:19:08.701 --> 00:19:09.767
"Well, I guess
we've got to start

00:19:09.767 --> 00:19:11.067
printing those campaign posters.

00:19:11.067 --> 00:19:12.501
Here we go."

00:19:12.501 --> 00:19:15.367
I felt like he was this close to
using the word "abracadabra."

00:19:15.367 --> 00:19:17.267
Did you --
When Trump was talking.

00:19:17.267 --> 00:19:19.534
Trump also suggested
a pretty interesting theory

00:19:19.534 --> 00:19:22.267
on why the FBI searched
his house in the first place.

00:19:22.267 --> 00:19:23.567
Listen to this.

00:19:23.567 --> 00:19:25.968
-Because of what they did,
the severity of the FBI

00:19:25.968 --> 00:19:29.767
coming and raiding Mar-a-Lago,
were they looking for the

00:19:29.767 --> 00:19:31.901
Hillary Clinton e-mails
that were deleted?

00:19:31.901 --> 00:19:33.767
But they are around someplace.

00:19:33.767 --> 00:19:35.400
Were they looking for the --
-Wait, wait.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.200
You're not saying you had it.
-No, no.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:38.701
They may be saying --

00:19:38.701 --> 00:19:40.901
They may have thought
that it was in there.

00:19:45.234 --> 00:19:47.133
-At that point, even QAnon
people were like,

00:19:47.133 --> 00:19:48.868
"Okay, that conspiracy seems
a little nuts.

00:19:48.868 --> 00:19:51.267
That's a little much for us."

00:19:51.267 --> 00:19:52.400
You've got to give Trump
credit, though.

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:54.100
He knows how to say
something so crazy

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:55.901
that it actually makes
the last crazy thing he said

00:19:55.901 --> 00:19:57.167
seem normal.

00:19:57.167 --> 00:19:58.667
You know, right?
You know what I'm saying?

00:19:58.667 --> 00:20:00.801
Trump had a lot to say about
the search of Mar-a-Lago,

00:20:00.801 --> 00:20:02.667
including something
the FBI took from him.

00:20:02.667 --> 00:20:03.801
Watch this.

00:20:03.801 --> 00:20:06.734
-They took a lot.
I think they took my will.

00:20:06.734 --> 00:20:08.801
I found out yesterday.
I said, "Where is it?"

00:20:08.801 --> 00:20:10.934
-Am I in it?
-I think they took my will.

00:20:10.934 --> 00:20:12.000
That could cause
a lot of problems.

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:13.067
-I know.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:17.067
-The FBI was like, "Oh,
you mean the piece of paper

00:20:17.067 --> 00:20:18.567
with the Sharpie treasure map?

00:20:18.567 --> 00:20:20.868
Yeah, we did --"

00:20:20.868 --> 00:20:22.467
A minute later,
Melania handed it back

00:20:22.467 --> 00:20:24.634
and was like, "Sorry,
I was just checking something.

00:20:24.634 --> 00:20:26.167
"We're all good."

00:20:26.167 --> 00:20:28.501
Switching gears,
tonight on Amazon,

00:20:28.501 --> 00:20:30.868
there was another
Thursday night football game.

00:20:30.868 --> 00:20:33.934
And, apparently, Amazon -- Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:20:33.934 --> 00:20:37.434
Apparently, Amazon has a policy
not to show ads for alcohol,

00:20:37.434 --> 00:20:39.267
which means there are no
beer commercials

00:20:39.267 --> 00:20:40.734
during their football games.

00:20:40.734 --> 00:20:42.634
Yeah. I don't know why
Amazon does that,

00:20:42.634 --> 00:20:44.033
because drunk people
ordering stuff

00:20:44.033 --> 00:20:46.734
on Amazon is
90% of their business.

00:20:48.801 --> 00:20:50.167
Speaking of football,

00:20:50.167 --> 00:20:51.601
there's so many games
to keep up with this weekend,

00:20:51.601 --> 00:20:53.167
so I wanted to
take a moment to look at

00:20:53.167 --> 00:20:55.267
this week's big matches
and take some picks.

00:20:55.267 --> 00:20:57.934
It's time for "Tonight Show
Weekend Football Lock Box."

